From 007951ae8c35ff087d32a0a65d49de71a49c4c15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert Christie <rgcgeog@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:25:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gpgpu): GPUFFT1D lengths up to 65536 (block scratch
 holds at least one transform)

GPU_FFT1D_MAX_LENGTH is now 2^16, independent of the 2048 bound GPUFFT2D and GPUConvolution keep
sharing (GPU_FFT_MAX_LENGTH). Every pass is global-memory (no workgroup storage), so the length was
only bounded by the shared constant; the chunked path's block scratch was capped at 4096 complex
rows, which would hold zero transforms of 8192, so it now holds max(4096, length) rows within the
binding/buffer limits. getGPUFFTLengthReason takes an optional maxLength.
